{"accessed_at":"2026-11-08T05:07:36.413Z","response":"Medium data (https://www.jcm.riken.jp/cgi-bin/jcm/jcm_grmd?GRMD=1130)\nciteturn14view0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://www.jcm.riken.jp/cgi-bin/jcm/jcm_grmd?GRMD=1130\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 63\nL0: # Medium data\nL1: \nL2: Search for medium no. = [1130].\nL3: \nL4: * * *\nL5: \nL6: Unless otherwise stated, sterilize media by autoclaving at 121°C for 15 min.\nL7: \nL8: * * *\nL9: \nL10: 1130   YCFA MEDIUM\nL11: Tryptone (BD-Difco)  | ` 10.0    `  | g\nL12: Yeast extract (BD-Difco)  | ` 2.5    `  | g\nL13: NaHCO_{3}  | ` 4.0    `  | g\nL14: Glucose  | ` 2.0    `  | g\nL15: Maltose  | ` 2.0    `  | g\nL16: Cellobiose  | ` 2.0    `  | g\nL17: L-Cysteine·HCl·H_{2}O  | ` 1.0    `  | g\nL18: Mineral solution I (see below)  | ` 150.0    `  | ml\nL19: Mineral solution II (see below)  | ` 150.0    `  | ml\nL20: Resazurin  | ` 1.0    `  | mg\nL21: VFA mix (see below)  | ` 6.2    `  | ml\nL22: Hemin solution (see below)  | ` 10.0    `  | ml\nL23: Vitamin solution I (see below)  | ` 1.0    `  | ml\nL24: Distilled water  | ` 660.0    `  | ml\nL25: Adjust pH to 7.45.\nL26: After autoclaving, add filter-sterilized 1.0 ml Vitamin solution II (see below).\nL27: Mineral solution I:\nL28: K_{2}HPO_{4}  | ` 3.0    `  | g\nL29: Distilled water  | ` 1.0    `  | L\nL30: Mineral solution II:\nL31: KH_{2}PO_{4}  | ` 3.0    `  | g\nL32: (NH_{4})_{2}SO_{4}  | ` 6.0    `  | g\nL33: NaCl  | ` 6.0    `  | g\nL34: MgSO_{4}·7H_{2}O  | ` 0.6    `  | g\nL35: CaCl_{2}·2H_{2}O  | ` 0.6    `  | g\nL36: Distilled water  | ` 1.0    `  | L\nL37: VFA mix:\nL38: Acetic acid  | ` 17.0    `  | ml\nL39: Propionic acid  | ` 6.0    `  | ml\nL40: n-Valeric acid  | ` 1.0    `  | ml\nL41: iso-Valeric acid  | ` 1.0    `  | ml\nL42: iso-Butyric acid  | ` 1.0    `  | ml\nL43: 10 N NaOH  | ` 26.0    `  | ml\nL44: Hemin solution:\nL45: KOH  | ` 0.28   `  | g\nL46: Ethanol  | ` 25.0    `  | ml\nL47: Hemin  | ` 0.1    `  | g\nL48: Adjust volume to 100 ml with distilled water.\nL49: Vitamin solution I:\nL50: Biotin  | ` 5.0    `  | mg\nL51: Vitamin B_{1}_{2}  | ` 5.0    `  | mg\nL52: p-Aminobenzoic acid  | ` 15.0    `  | mg\nL53: Folic acid  | ` 25.0    `  | mg\nL54: Pyridoxine·HCl  | ` 75.0    `  | mg\nL55: Distilled water  | ` 500.0    `  | ml\nL56: Vitamin solution II:\nL57: Thiamine·HCl  | ` 25.0    `  | mg\nL58: Riboflavin  | ` 25.0    `  | mg\nL59: Distilled water  | ` 500.0    `  | ml\nL60: * * *\nL61: \nL62: Copyright © 2026 Microbe Division (JCM) - All Rights Reserved\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nMedium data (https://www.jcm.riken.jp/cgi-bin/jcm/jcm_grmd?GRMD=393)\nciteturn14view1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 2 months ago; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://www.jcm.riken.jp/cgi-bin/jcm/jcm_grmd?GRMD=393\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 17\nL0: # Medium data\nL1: \nL2: Search for medium no. = [393].\nL3: \nL4: * * *\nL5: \nL6: Unless otherwise stated, sterilize media by autoclaving at 121°C for 15 min.\nL7: \nL8: * * *\nL9: \nL10: 393   DESULFOBACTERIUM NIACINI MEDIUM\nL11: \nL12: Use Medium No. 【0†383】 supplemented with 13.5 g/L (final) NaCl and 2.2 g/L (final) MgCl_{2}·6H_{2}O, with 0.725 g/L sodium nicotinate (filter-sterilized) instead of sodium lactate, and without yeast extract.\nL13: \nL14: * * *\nL15: \nL16: Copyright © 2026 Microbe Division (JCM) - All Rights Reserved\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nMedium data (https://www.jcm.riken.jp/cgi-bin/jcm/jcm_grmd?GRMD=600)\nciteturn14view2 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last year; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://www.jcm.riken.jp/cgi-bin/jcm/jcm_grmd?GRMD=600\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 41\nL0: # Medium data\nL1: \nL2: Search for medium no. = [600].\nL3: \nL4: * * *\nL5: \nL6: Unless otherwise stated, sterilize media by autoclaving at 121°C for 15 min.\nL7: \nL8: * * *\nL9: \nL10: 600   G5G6 MEDIUM\nL11: Solution A:\nL12: Na_{2}HPO_{4}·12H_{2}O ` 0.5    ` g\nL13: KH_{2}PO_{4} ` 0.65   ` g\nL14: FeCl_{2} solution (see Medium No. 【0†187】) ` 1.0    ` ml\nL15: Trace element solution (see below) ` 1.0    ` ml\nL16: Resazurin ` 0.5    ` mg\nL17: Distilled water ` 880.0    ` ml\nL18: Solution B:\nL19: CaCl_{2}·2H_{2}O ` 0.11   ` g\nL20: MgCl_{2}·6H_{2}O ` 0.1    ` g\nL21: Distilled water ` 50.0    ` ml\nL22: Solution C:\nL23: NH_{4}HCO_{3} ` 0.44   ` g\nL24: NaHCO_{3} ` 3.73   ` g\nL25: L-Cysteine·HCl·H_{2}O ` 0.175  ` g\nL26: Distilled water ` 50.0    ` ml\nL27: Prepare all solutions and autoclave under a N_{2} atmosphere. After cooling, combine the solutions and replace the gas phase with a N_{2}-CO_{2} (4:1, v/v) gas mixture. Then, add the following autoclaved or *filter-sterilized solutions to the medium:\nL28: 1.0 M NaNO_{3} solution ` 10.0    ` ml\nL29: Trace vitamins* (see Medium No. 【1†197】) ` 10.0    ` ml\nL30: Vitamin B_{1}_{2} solution* (see Medium No. 【2†403】) ` 1.0    ` ml\nL31: Check the final pH to be around 7.3.\nL32: Distribute appropriate amount of the medium into culture vessels under the same gas mixture (e.g., 40.0 ml in 120 ml serum bottle) and seal with Viton rubber stoppers. Finally add per liter the following solution from an anaerobic stock (autoclaved):\nL33: 5.0 mM Toluene (water-saturated) ` 40.0    ` ml\nL34: Trace element solution:\nL35: Trace element solution (see Medium No. 【0†187】) ` 1.0    ` L\nL36: AlCl_{3}·6H_{2}O ` 10.0    ` mg\nL37: Comment: For strain JCM 14632, incubate with a 5-10% inoculum. When toluene is depleted, re-add the toluene solution (normally every 3 to 4 days, until enough cell growth is seen).\nL38: * * *\nL39: \nL40: Copyright © 2025 Microbe Division (JCM) - All Rights Reserved\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n88: SULFOLOBUS MEDIUM (https://www.dsmz.de/microorganisms/medium/pdf/DSMZ_Medium88.pdf)\nciteturn14view3 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: application/pdf; Number of pages: 2; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://www.dsmz.de/microorganisms/medium/pdf/DSMZ_Medium88.pdf\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 58\nL0@P0: 88: SULFOLOBUS MEDIUM\nL1@P0: (NH4)2SO4 1.30 g\nL2@P0: KH2PO4 0.28 g\nL3@P0: MgSO4 x 7 H2O 0.25 g\nL4@P0: CaCl2 x 2 H2O 0.07 g\nL5@P0: FeCl3 x 6 H2O 0.02 g\nL6@P0: Allen's trace element solution 10.00 ml\nL7@P0: Yeast extract (OXOID) 1.00 g\nL8@P0: Distilled water 1000.00 ml\nL9@P0: Dissolve ingredients (except yeast extract or other substrates), adjust pH of the salt\nL10@P0: solution at room temperature to 2.0 using 10 N H2SO4 and autoclave. Yeast extract and\nL11@P0: other organic substrates are sterilized separately by autoclaving of a 10% (w/v) stock\nL12@P0: solution at neutral pH.\nL13@P0: For DSM 5348: Omit yeast extract and supplement medium with 0.50 g/l powdered sulfur\nL14@P0: and 20.00 g/l sulfide ore (e.g., pyrite). Sterilize sulfur separately by steaming for 3 hours\nL15@P0: on each of 3 successive days (see medium 35) and ore by heating at 150°C overnight. Add\nL16@P0: sulfur and ore aseptically to the autoclaved medium.\nL17@P0: For DSM 5389, DSM 7519, DSM 12421: Adjust pH of medium to 3.0 - 3.5.\nL18@P0: For DSM 6482, DSM 10039, DSM 104736: Reduce the amount of yeast extract to 0.20 g/l\nL19@P0: and supplement the medium with 5.00 g/l powdered sulfur. Sterilize sulfur separately by\nL20@P0: steaming for 3 hours on each of 3 successive days (see medium 35) and add aseptically to\nL21@P0: the autoclaved medium.\nL22@P0: For DSM 9789, DSM 9790: Use 2.00 g/l yeast extract and adjust pH of medium to 1.0 by\nL23@P0: using 300.00 ml 0.5 M H2SO4 and 700.00 ml distilled water for the dissolving of salts.\nL24@P0: For DSM 16993: Supplement medium with 1.00 g/l D-glucose and 1.00 g/l Casamino acids.\nL25@P0: Adjust pH of the completed medium to 3.0.\nL26@P0: For DSM 18247: Modified, with 0.5% yeast extract; solidified by 0.7% Gelrite; pH:9.0\nL27@P0: For DSM 18786: Use only 0.10 g/l yeast extract and supplement medium with 10.00 g/l\nL28@P0: sulfide ore (e.g., chalcopyrite). Sterilize ore by heating at 150°C overnight. Adjust the pH\nL29@P0: of the medium to 0.8.\nL30@P0: For DSM 29038: Supplement medium with 3.00 g/l K2S4O6 added to the autoclaved\nL31@P0: medium from a stock solution sterilized by filtration. Adjust pH of completed medium to\nL32@P0: 2.5.\nL33@P0: For DSM 29099: Use only 0.20 g/l yeast extract and supplement medium with 1.00 g/l\nL34@P0: D-glucose and 10.00 g/l powdered sulfur. Sterilize sulfur separately by steaming for 3\nL35@P0: hours on each of 3 successive days (see medium 35) and add aseptically to the autoclaved\nL36@P0: medium. Adjust pH of final medium to 2.5 - 3.0.\nL37@P0-1: © 2022 DSMZ - All rights reserved Page 1 of 288: SULFOLOBUS MEDIUM\nL38@P1: For DSM 45263: Adjust pH of medium to 7.5\nL39@P1: For DSM 111728: Use only 0.50 g/l yeast extract and supplement medium with 10.00 g/l\nL40@P1: powdered sulfur. Sterilize sulfur separately by steaming for 3 hours on each of 3\nL41@P1: successive days (see medium 35) and add aseptically to the autoclaved medium. Adjust\nL42@P1: the pH of the final medium to 2.5.\nL43@P1: For DSM 112778: Supplement medium with 0.50 g/l powdered sulfur and 20.00 g/l sulfide\nL44@P1: ore (e.g., pyrite). Sterilize sulfur separately by steaming for 3 hours on each of 3\nL45@P1: successive days (see medium 35) and ore by heating at 150°C overnight. Add sulfur and\nL46@P1: ore aseptically to the autoclaved medium. Adjust the pH of the medium to 3.0.\nL47@P1: Allen's trace element solution (from medium 88)\nL48@P1: MnCl2 x 4 H2O 180.00 mg\nL49@P1: Na2B4O7 x 10 H2O 450.00 mg\nL50@P1: ZnSO4 x 7 H2O 22.00 mg\nL51@P1: CuCl2 x 2 H2O 5.00 mg\nL52@P1: Na2MoO4 x 2 H2O 3.00 mg\nL53@P1: VOSO4 x 2 H2O 3.00 mg\nL54@P1: CoSO4 x 7 H2O 1.00 mg\nL55@P1: Distilled water 1000.00 ml\nL56@P1: Adjust pH of final solution to 2 with 1 N HCl.\nL57@P1: © 2022 DSMZ - All rights reserved Page 2 of 2\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n60: NEOMOORELLA MEDIUM (https://www.dsmz.de/microorganisms/medium/pdf/DSMZ_Medium60.pdf)\nciteturn14view4 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 3 months ago; Content type: application/pdf; Number of pages: 2; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://www.dsmz.de/microorganisms/medium/pdf/DSMZ_Medium60.pdf\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 43\nL0@P0: 60: NEOMOORELLA MEDIUM\nL1@P0: Final pH: 6.9\nL2@P0: Final volume: 1003 ml\nL3@P0: Solution A 843.00 ml\nL4@P0: Solution B 50.00 ml\nL5@P0: Solution C 50.00 ml\nL6@P0: Solution D 40.00 ml\nL7@P0: Solution E 10.00 ml\nL8@P0: Solution F 10.00 ml\nL9@P0: Sparge solution A with 100% CO2 gas for 30 - 45 min to make it anoxic, then distribute\nL10@P0: under same gas atmosphere into anoxic Hungate-type tubes or serum vials and autoclave.\nL11@P0: Autoclave separately solutions B, C, E and F under 100% N2 gas, and solution D under 80%\nL12@P0: N2 and 20% CO2 gas atmosphere. To complete the medium appropriate amounts of\nL13@P0: solutions B to F are added to the sterile solution A in the sequence as indicated. Adjust pH\nL14@P0: of the complete medium to 6.9, if necessary.\nL15@P0: Solution A\nL16@P0: MgSO4 x 7 H2O 0.10 g\nL17@P0: (NH4)2SO4 0.50 g\nL18@P0: Fe(NH4)2(SO4)2 0.04 g\nL19@P0: Na2MoO4 x 2 H2O (0.1% w/v) 2.40 ml\nL20@P0: Na2SeO3 x 5 H2O (0.1% w/v) 0.15 ml\nL21@P0: Tryptone 5.00 g\nL22@P0: Yeast extract 5.00 g\nL23@P0: Sodium resazurin (0.1% w/v) 0.50 ml\nL24@P0: Distilled water 840.00 ml\nL25@P0: Solution B\nL26@P0: K2HPO4 7.00 g\nL27@P0: KH2PO4 4.50 g\nL28@P0: Distilled water 50.00 ml\nL29@P0: Solution C\nL30@P0: Glucose 18.00 g\nL31@P0: Distilled water 50.00 ml\nL32@P0-1: © 2026 DSMZ - All rights reserved Page 1 of 260: NEOMOORELLA MEDIUM\nL33@P1: Solution D\nL34@P1: Na2CO3 2.00 g\nL35@P1: Distilled water 40.00 ml\nL36@P1: Solution E\nL37@P1: L-Cysteine HCl x H2O 0.30 g\nL38@P1: Distilled water 10.00 ml\nL39@P1: Solution F\nL40@P1: Na2S x 9 H2O 0.30 g\nL41@P1: Distilled water 10.00 ml\nL42@P1: © 2026 DSMZ - All rights reserved Page 2 of 2\n"}
